"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-308_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reproduced 2026-11-04 on origin/main fe6c2100292 (macOS, py3.12): running test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py::test_cli_passed_but_unsigned_is_exit_11_with_byte_identical_stderr then test_verify_completion_facades.py::test_cli_llm_error_is_clean_exit_one in one process fails the second with 'ValueError: I/O operation on closed file' from rebar._logging's StreamHandler(sys.stderr) (warning from _seam._apply_authorship). The verify test alone passes 3 of 3. Under make verify -n 4 both failed when they shared worker gw0. Seen while verifying exemplary-silty-tuatara, which does not touch logging.","timestamp":1793805807310005001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Reproduced again 2026-11-04 while verifying cliffy-nonliving-blacklab: the same 2 tests failed in make verify (load average ~30, macOS, py3.12), and running the 2 modules together fails both, 2 of 27, with the change's 3 source files restored to origin/main fe6c2100292. Unrelated to that change, which touches only the write divergence guard.","timestamp":1793805835922324001}],"created_at":1793804207360410001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e81db9a2-6408-404f-b121-2816db935f93","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"571b-f552-5fa7-4b74"},{"link_uuid":"ebdb83f1-3d00-4794-ae94-35d6b7c52843","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"eac3-3f1b-69bb-414e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOn 2026-11-04, `make verify` on macOS failed 2 default-tier tests whose asserted stderr starts with a `--- Logging error ---` traceback (`ValueError: I/O operation on closed file`):\n\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py::test_cli_passed_but_unsigned_is_exit_11_with_byte_identical_stderr`\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py::test_cli_llm_error_is_clean_exit_one`\n\nThis breaks every local `make verify` whenever both land on one xdist worker. The failing record is the `rebar._commands._seam._apply_authorship` warning `authorship: signing SKIPPED ...`, emitted while the test seeds its ticket.\n\nReproduced on origin/main 1c8a67702f8: running the plan-review test then the verify-completion test in one process (`-p no:randomly -p no:xdist`) fails the second, 3 of 3 runs; the verify test alone passes.\n\n### Root cause (confirmed by probe)\n\nA scratch pytest plugin listed the `rebar` logger's handlers after each test. After the plan-review test, the handler stamped `_rebar_stderr_handler` holds that test's `capsys` `CaptureIO`, now `closed=True`; it is still attached during the next test.\n\n- Production: `install_stderr_handler` (`src/rebar/_logging.py:81`) builds `logging.StreamHandler(sys.stderr)`, freezing the stderr object current at install time. It is idempotent by marker (`_logging.py:73-75`), so later `rebar._cli.main` calls (`src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:316-318`) never rebind it. Any in-process caller of `main` whose `sys.stderr` is later replaced or closed (pytest capture, `contextlib.redirect_stderr`, an embedding application) gets diagnostics written to a dead or wrong stream. The polluting test in the pair is the plan-review test (the first in-process `main` call under `capsys`); in the full tier, it is whichever CLI test calls `main` first on that worker.\n- Test: the plan-review test asserts byte-identical stderr, but its capture also includes `_seed`'s output (line 85, before `main` at line 87). Whether seeding logs anything depends on whether an earlier test already installed the handler. A probe that rebinds the handler to the current `sys.stderr` made the pair pass in order A,B, and made the plan-review test fail in order B,A with the seeding warning as an extra first line.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. Production fix: make the entrypoint handler resolve `sys.stderr` at write time instead of at install time. Add a `logging.StreamHandler` subclass in `src/rebar/_logging.py` whose `stream` is a property returning the current `sys.stderr`, the same pattern the standard library uses for its last-resort handler (`logging._StderrHandler`). `install_stderr_handler` installs it in place of `StreamHandler(sys.stderr)`; the marker, idempotency, level resolution, formatter, and stderr-only contract stay unchanged. This fits because the documented contract (`_logging.py` docstring) is that entrypoints emit diagnostics to stderr, meaning the process's stderr, and install once per process; binding lazily honours both and removes the stale reference for all 4 entrypoints (CLI, MCP server, reconciler, compact sweep) at once.\n2. Test fix: in the plan-review test, discard captured output after `_seed` (`capsys.readouterr()`), so its byte-identical assertion covers only the CLI command's stderr, which is what its docstring says it pins.\n\nNo autouse fixture, no new mechanism, no test reordering, retry, or skip.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_logging.py`: add the lazy-stderr handler class; use it in `install_stderr_handler`.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py`: drain seeding output before invoking `main`.\n- `tests/unit/test_logging_stderr_target.py` (new): regression tests.\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `tests/unit/test_logging_stderr_target.py`, isolating the `rebar` logger with `monkeypatch.setattr` on its `handlers` list and level (no autouse fixture):\n\n- Happy path: install the handler while `sys.stderr` is buffer A, close A, replace `sys.stderr` with buffer B, log a warning on a `rebar.*` logger. Assert B contains the formatted line and no `--- Logging error ---`. Fails before the fix (record goes to closed A, the logging-error traceback lands in B).\n- Edge: a second `install_stderr_handler` call after the swap still leaves exactly 1 marked handler, and output follows the current `sys.stderr`.\n\nThen run the 2 facade tests together in both orders, both facade modules together, the CLI facade/contract modules with exact-stderr assertions (`tests/interfaces/facades/`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/`, `tests/interfaces/queries/test_validate_compute.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_store.py`, `tests/unit/test_logging_level.py`, `tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate/`), plus `make lint` and `make typecheck`, with the worktree `.venv/bin` first on `PATH` and Jira variables unset. CI's `Verified` vote covers the full default tier.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The handler that outlives the test is identified, with the code that installs it: the marked handler from `install_stderr_handler` (`src/rebar/_logging.py`), installed by `rebar._cli.main`; recorded in a ticket comment.\n- [ ] The 2 tests above pass when run together in one process in either order (`pytest -p no:randomly -p no:xdist <A> <B>` and `<B> <A>`), both exit 0.\n- [ ] Both facade modules together pass with `-p no:randomly -p no:xdist` (exit 0).\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_logging_stderr_target.py` fails on origin/main's `_logging.py` and passes after the fix (both runs recorded in a ticket comment).\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0, and the change gets `Verified +1` in Gerrit, which runs the full default tier.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_logging.py","reason":"resolve sys.stderr at write time in the entrypoint handler"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py","reason":"drain seeding output before asserting byte-identical CLI stderr"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_logging_stderr_target.py","reason":"new regression tests for the stale-stream handler"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","eac3-3f1b-69bb-414e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"3382cd20-7533-44a5-ba9f-1e61d11c5adf","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"cded-334b-a742-4082","ticket_type":"bug","title":"CLI facade tests fail on a logging handler bound to an earlier test's closed stderr","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b7d6bca1-5a02-4b44-9c97-32b71cd0ec41","e81db9a2-6408-404f-b121-2816db935f93","ed290ded-ecc7-47f4-96de-cb7777d1e9a5","ebdb83f1-3d00-4794-ae94-35d6b7c52843","1e8e539e-bb0e-4115-b719-d446382c8344","d78c5607-1bc7-46aa-bc07-7331eaf42a4c","2999102d-1b9a-47c8-9b3b-edbc1d6f5782","1a6d4d38-3759-492b-9c3f-92407aebce4d","3382cd20-7533-44a5-ba9f-1e61d11c5adf","202f8a13-f6d8-499d-8a6e-dc6b4d022b39"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793812642464829002,"uuid":"7455c8db-860e-4984-b8cc-00bc6278ee9f"}